                    "message": "@patrick@stwcx.xyz could you re-review please?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/OperatingClockSpeed.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Right now \"WriteFailure\" is only used by one interface.  I'm not sure if I like us adding that more often.  It seems like all of your commits you're starting to add this.\n\nWhat is a caller supposed to do with a WriteFailure?  If we can't define the expected caller action, or we can't map this cleanly back to some expected Redfish response, I'd rather we eat this in your daemon."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/OperatingClockSpeed.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the feedback. I understand now \u2014 D-Bus errors are for the caller's code path, not for debug-level distinctions. I'll remove WriteFailure from both the property setters and the Reset method, and have the daemon swallow hardware write failures (logged to journal)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/OperatingClockSpeed.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 58,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there a reason to restricted it to Accelerator?  Should we allow any Inventory.Item?  Should we allow Cpu and/or CpuCore and/or Dimm?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/OperatingClockSpeed.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 58,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, thanks for the remind."
                }
            ],
